WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.380
My passionate idol activities,

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:07.110
Aikatsu! is about to start! {sounds like aigatsu}

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:10.460
So far on Aikatsu!

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:15.990
I'm Hoshimiya Ichigo, a third-year at the idol school Starlight Academy.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.190
We all use Aikatsu cards to do our idol activities.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:24.540
During the one year I spent in America,

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.630
a new school called Dream Academy, or DreAca for short, was founded.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:33.500
One of the students there, the massively new idol Otoshiro Seira-chan,

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:37.390
performed a Constellation Appeal in her very first concert. {split}

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:43.640
I somehow managed to perform a Constellation Appeal too, but I ended up losing to Seira-chan.

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:50.280
Seira-chan's producer, Saegusa Kii-chan, made her idol debut while continuing to be a producer.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:53.030
DreAca's pretty amazing!

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.530
However, our Shibuki Ran, the Beautiful Blade,

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:02.000
just recently pulled off a Constellation Appeal in Spicy Ageha's Constellation Dress. {split}

00:01:02.830 --> 00:01:06.250
Starlight Academy won't go down that easily.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:13.460
They're all wonderful rivals whose Aikatsu will raise everyone to ever greater heights. {you a suck}

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.610
My Aikatsu is getting more and more passionate! {exclamation point}

00:01:18.790 --> 00:01:22.310
Extremely Naughty Police Chief, scene 210! {to match the sign}

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.390
And... action!

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.860
Even as police chief...

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.360
And... cut!

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:40.410
Good job!

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.740
Thank you.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:45.200
Kiriya.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.430
Headmistress Orihime.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:53.010
Could I have some of your time after this?

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:56.720
Those two over there want to have a meeting with us.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.560
Good work today.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.280
They've come with a pretty amazing request.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.230
They said they wanted to make a new TV drama with you, Kiriya.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.980
A drama with me?!

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.920
You're writing the story for a drama?!

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:57.240
And there's an audition for it?

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:58.250
Yeah.

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.470
What kind of drama will it be?

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:04.680
It'll be for these chocolates that'll be on the market soon.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:06.730
So many!

00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:08.260
Aikatsu Choco?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:09.740
Yeah.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:14.570
They wanted to air a special drama at the same time these chocolates are released.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:16.650
That's what they told me.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.260
Aoi, you're awesome!

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:22.690
Says the girl looking straight at the chocolate.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.010
Sit. {I imagined this as a dog command}

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.590
I'll open it for you.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:37.210
They must've given you that offer because every drama you're in ends up being popular.

00:04:37.530 --> 00:04:38.490
Yeah.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.220
They said that too.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:44.830
They also wanted to be able to say that the drama was created by a real idol.

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:49.190
I see.

00:04:49.190 --> 00:04:52.730
Just the fact that you're behind it builds all sorts of hype.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:56.310
So, what kind of drama do they want you to make?

00:04:56.830 --> 00:04:59.190
Um, let's see...

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.360
What about one called "Chocolate Detective"?

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:08.750
When she eats the chocolate, an idea pops out.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.080
That sounds great.

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:14.960
Wasshoi, wasshoi, it gets me so pumped up!

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.130
Right.

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:20.630
So the Chocolate Detective solves mysteries.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:25.800
If there's a mystery, the TV audience will be sure to watch until the end.

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.990
Wasshoi wasshoi, indeed!

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:33.450
I'm so glad we asked you for ideas.

00:05:33.450 --> 00:05:37.850
Now we'll wasshoi you up a detective office set for you to use!

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.270
Okay.

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:41.310
I'm looking forward to the audition.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.400
That's pretty much how the meeting went.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:49.470
A detective who pops out an idea whenever she eats chocolate. {I'm going to keep doing this to keep to chocopop}

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:51.370
Sounds like it'll be cute.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.160
Yeah, yeah!

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.310
So anyway,

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:02.460
let's all enter this audition together. {isn't it kinda of weird for Aoi to be in the audition herself}

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.420
Of course!

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:06.670
Are you in it just for the chocolate?

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.510
Of course!

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.190
Wait, no...

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:13.390
Of course I'd want to audition for something you thought up, Aoi.

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.530
Really?

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.580
Really, really!

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.330
I wonder what the audition'll be like.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:29.020
I don't know the specifics of what they have planned either.

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:31.410
The scenario's being handed in day-of, too.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:33.870
I'm looking forward to it!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.530
I as well.

00:06:35.530 --> 00:06:39.670
Aoi-sama, thank you for inviting me to this audition.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:41.080
No problem.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.340
I'm glad you all came.

00:06:43.340 --> 00:06:44.300
You too, Yurika-chan.

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:51.680
The famous Austrian vampire, Carmilla-sama, drank one cup of chocolate every day as part of her routine. {I swear we've had to look this name up before}

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.890
And if Yurika-sama passes this audition,

00:06:55.570 --> 00:06:57.060
I'll suck the chocolate!

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:59.870
They're balls of chocolate, so you can't suck them.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.310
What did you say?!

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:04.320
We won't lose either.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.090
Seira-chan and Kii-chan!

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:09.300
We were invited too.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:13.210
This is the first time either of us has entered a drama audition.

00:07:13.210 --> 00:07:15.080
Excite excite excite! {eh}

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.880
Seira-chan, let's do our best!

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:18.540
Yeah.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:21.780
I'll be a full step ahead of you today as well.

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:23.790
If you're <i>do</i>, then I'm <i>re</i>.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:26.090
Fine, then I'm <i>mi</i>!

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:29.530
Then I'm <i>fa</i>!

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.590
Then I'm <i>fa</i>-sharp!

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.590
Sh-Sharp?!

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.840
In that case, I'm <i>so</i>! <i>So!</i>{that second so was Seira}

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.370
Then I'm <i>so</i>-sharp! {too bad they didn't have her be mi-sharp or something)}{are you a baka}

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.100
They sure get along well.

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.080
What's with the sharps? {guessing here}

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.590
I'll be <i>la</i> instead!

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:40.670
It's really something special.

00:07:40.670 --> 00:07:41.880
There it is!

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.060
A real "something special"!

00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.100
If that's how it is...

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:47.690
I'll suck your blood.

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:49.580
The real thing!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:53.030
You're the Yurika-sama who sleeps in a coffin-offin-offin! {.......}{I don't mind what you did, but you had one extra}

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.870
Coffin-offin-offin?

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:02.640
Why, we are all the real deals!

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:04.460
There's the Kitaouji Theater!

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:06.950
Love you!

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:09.010
There! Love you!

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:11.180
Everyone's into it.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:12.720
Especially those two.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:13.890
<i>Do!</i>

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:14.800
<i>Re!</i>

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.650
<i>Mi!</i>

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:16.520
<i>Fa!</i>

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:18.240
How long are you going to keep that up?

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.540
<i>So!</i>

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:19.170
Let's go.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:20.640
Okay.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:28.490
Anyway, I'm looking forward to the audition that you're pro-pro-producing, Aoi-chan.

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:29.360
Thanks! {I don't know}

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:31.850
I'm sure it'll be cute.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:32.730
Yeah.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:38.310
Aoi's Chocolate Detective drama's 
cuteness will definitely be ok-ok-okay!

00:08:48.070 --> 00:08:49.360
Okay? {this was a typo but maybe...}{you're making me tired}

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:59.200
How... subdued.

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.310
It's very Showa.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:06.710
Chocolate-Bar Detective audition, scene 12!

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:08.610
And... action!

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:13.520
Yo.

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.730
Office of the Chocolate-Bar Detective.

00:09:17.450 --> 00:09:18.330
Uh-huh.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:20.510
Okay.

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.190
Got it.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:28.080
Miss, we have a new case.

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:30.360
Could you tell me the details?

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:33.760
Harada-san from 3-chome wants an 
investigation into someone's history.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:34.550
A-yo.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:37.800
All right. Chocolate-Bar Detective, dispatch!

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.310
We'll take care of it.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.900
Cut!

00:09:43.900 --> 00:09:45.480
Okay!

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:51.650
What a drab drama.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:55.900
Is this the kind of chocolate detective you had in mind?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:03.670
Otome wanted something more chocolatey.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:07.130
I thought it'd be more of a "choco-choco" kind of drama.

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:07.940
Here.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:11.290
Sounds good.

00:10:11.730 --> 00:10:14.110
That's it! Just like that! {Otome and Ichigo should pair. they'd've won}

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:14.710
Huh?

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:21.800
What I had in mind was something more like the "choco-choco" kind of drama you mentioned, Otome.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:24.570
Ah, I see!

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:27.510
The Starlight Queen always knows what to do.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:28.590
Wasshoi!

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:30.160
I heard everything.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.930
Both the set and the script were way too gritty.

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:37.560
When we old geezers heard Kiriya-chan's wasshoi idea,

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.360
we wasshoi didn't get it at all!

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.870
Wasshoi?

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.370
Don't you say that when you hoist a festival float? {sure I guess}

00:10:45.690 --> 00:10:52.880
Kiriya-chan, could you please give us your ideas one more time?

00:10:53.870 --> 00:10:54.700
Yes!

00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:01.340
First of all, I don't think we should use bar-shaped chocolate.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:04.610
Aikatsu chocolate is ball-shaped!

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.720
You're right on.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:12.540
Therefore, I think the detective should eat cute, ball-shaped chocolate.

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:13.730
Agreed!

00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:17.310
A Pop'n Pop chocolate detective!

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.410
I've got it!

00:11:22.410 --> 00:11:24.370
Why don't you call her the Chocopop Detective?

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.080
I like that!

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.330
Also, what you just did was pretty special.

00:11:29.050 --> 00:11:30.000
What I just did?

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.540
How an idea popped out right after eating the chocolate.

00:11:32.540 --> 00:11:33.680
Like this?

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:37.620
I've got it!

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:38.920
Right, just like that!

00:11:39.310 --> 00:11:40.670
That does look good.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:41.990
Right?

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:46.260
I believe I presented the same idea at our first meeting, too.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.890
Wasshoi...

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:49.250
Kii-chan,

00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:52.270
what do you think we should do about the set?

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:57.570
Right.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:03.570
I think it should be a cute room with chocolate and candy set into the walls.

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:09.790
Also, let's turn the old man into a bear.

00:12:10.190 --> 00:12:11.520
Cute!

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:12.840
I like it.

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:16.290
And we'll want some sort of cute catchphrase.

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.090
Yeah, yeah!

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.460
That's certainly important.

00:12:21.110 --> 00:12:26.970
I'll leave that wasshoi up to you to come up with during the audition!

00:12:27.290 --> 00:12:28.330
Yes!

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:34.270
We still have to figure out what the Chocopop Detective's outfit should be like.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:36.120
You're all so cute!

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:40.790
Now we've got the "choco-choco" feeling going on!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.260
Here.

00:12:44.300 --> 00:12:46.380
Take it easy on the feeding and eating.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:51.850
We're all paired up now.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:53.960
I'll be detective Ichigo's assistant.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:58.250
I'll be the detective.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.460
And I'll be the assistant.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:03.720
Otome's the detective!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.470
I still have a lot of learn, so please bear with me being your assistant.

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:11.750
I'm the detective?

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:16.850
Why does the great Yurika-sama have to be your assistant?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.390
I'm a vampire of six hundred years,

00:13:20.390 --> 00:13:24.320
so wouldn't it be natural for me to be the detective, and you the assistant?

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:26.410
So you want to switch?

00:13:26.410 --> 00:13:30.620
I think you'd look pretty cute in this detective outfit.

00:13:30.620 --> 00:13:33.290
Wh-What are you saying?

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:35.590
You look really cute in it yourself!

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:38.170
Is she trying to compliment her?

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.750
She is!

00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:43.820
Alright, I think I can pull this drama audition off.

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:45.800
No, I know I can!

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.010
Ok-ok-okay!

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.520
Let's get this audition rolling!

00:14:02.840 --> 00:14:07.650
Show us your acting skills, mixing in bits of ad-lib as you see fit.

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:10.910
Chocopop Detective audition, start!

00:14:20.740 --> 00:14:23.800
Yes, this is the Chocopop Detective office. {several of them}

00:14:24.350 --> 00:14:25.170
Okay.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:27.130
Alright.

00:14:27.130 --> 00:14:28.800
A new request?

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:29.970
Yeah.

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:33.810
Hello!

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:37.260
Welcome to the Chocopop Detective office!

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:42.520
So what's the request?

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.190
Well, you see...

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:47.020
I want you to help me find my stolen chocolate.

00:14:47.020 --> 00:14:48.730
Stolen chocolate?

00:14:48.730 --> 00:14:49.470
Yeah.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:15:00.040
The chocolate, made by a legendary Belgian patissier, was stolen en route to Japan. {good try, but our font doesn't have that}

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:02.840
I want you to help me find it.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:03.900
Okay!

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:05.040
Got it.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:07.090
We'll definitely find it for you!

00:15:07.520 --> 00:15:08.720
Leave it to us!

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.870
Seira-chan, that was great!

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:13.010
You're completely into your role!

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:18.070
Now that we're decided, let's go a-searching!

00:15:18.070 --> 00:15:19.480
Please hold on.

00:15:20.790 --> 00:15:23.980
We can search all we want, but it will be pointless if we don't have any clues.

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:30.860
It's true that without any hints, our detective here would be completely lost.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.740
I have a clue here.

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:39.120
If you solve this, you'll be able to see a map that shows where the stolen chocolate is. {what is this game mechanic}

00:15:39.690 --> 00:15:40.810
Let me see.

00:15:40.810 --> 00:15:42.500
Spot the differences?

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:47.880
We just need to find the three differences between the pictures and we'll be able to see the map.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.010
Alright, let's all think together!

00:15:58.260 --> 00:15:59.380
This is... {or "Uh..."}

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:01.640
Here...

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:02.900
Kii!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:11.030
I've got it!

00:16:11.680 --> 00:16:13.780
The first difference is here.

00:16:13.780 --> 00:16:15.380
The second one is here.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:16.930
And the last one is here. {I don't think the order matters}

00:16:18.510 --> 00:16:19.900
We did it!

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:20.910
Nice.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:26.920
Here's where the chocolate is.

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:27.830
Yes!

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.130
Good going, Kii-chan!

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.590
Alright, let's go look for the chocolate there.

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:34.800
Aye!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.860
Now, Chocopop Detective...

00:16:37.860 --> 00:16:39.930
Dispatch!

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:47.440
The stolen chocolate should be somewhere in this house.

00:16:48.210 --> 00:16:51.440
I'll give a bite of the chocolate to the detective who finds it first.

00:16:51.790 --> 00:16:53.180
Really?

00:16:53.180 --> 00:16:55.450
Okay, let's do this! {you're using alright a lot}

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:43.390
Yes!

00:18:43.390 --> 00:18:46.020
The stolen chocolate is in this room!

00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.450
It's probably in there.

00:18:50.450 --> 00:18:51.770
Yeah.

00:18:53.090 --> 00:18:54.400
Wait. {I didn't realize until this point}

00:18:54.400 --> 00:18:56.470
Everyone, wait there.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.530
I'll do the rest.

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.180
I feel like something's off.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.130
Ichigo.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:23.050
Kii.

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:25.650
Here!

00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:30.810
I've got it!

00:19:30.810 --> 00:19:32.660
What did you get?

00:19:32.660 --> 00:19:35.950
The chocolate was never actually stolen.

00:19:35.950 --> 00:19:37.270
Right?

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:38.400
Yeah!

00:19:39.370 --> 00:19:41.090
What do you mean?

00:19:41.090 --> 00:19:44.280
Explain it so vampires can understand.

00:19:44.690 --> 00:19:47.370
This isn't the thief's house!

00:19:47.370 --> 00:19:50.410
This is the house of the legendary 
patissier who made the chocolate!

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:55.410
The same one that was in the newspaper Kaede showed us.

00:19:56.810 --> 00:20:00.050
There were pictures of him hanging in this house.

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:03.830
We were tricked into finding the chocolate for her.

00:20:04.990 --> 00:20:08.360
In other words, the one who's really trying to steal the chocolate is...

00:20:10.130 --> 00:20:11.690
You!

00:20:21.960 --> 00:20:23.580
Exactly correct.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.700
Now that you've figured it out...

00:20:26.050 --> 00:20:27.910
Thanks for the chocolate!

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:28.830
Bye!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.410
We won't let you get away!

00:20:30.410 --> 00:20:31.200
Wait!

00:20:31.550 --> 00:20:33.710
You won't catch me!

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:57.610
Yummy!

00:21:00.670 --> 00:21:03.130
I wanted to have a bite too!

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.490
Sorry!

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:10.120
How Ichigo-tan ate it all in one bite is so Love You! {are we still capitalizing it} {yah}

00:21:11.140 --> 00:21:12.370
And with that,

00:21:13.240 --> 00:21:14.250
you've been caught!

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:16.880
Oh, give up!

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:21.000
No matter what the case may be...

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:23.760
We choco-choco wrap it up!

00:21:23.760 --> 00:21:25.820
Chocopop Detective!

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:27.610
Yay!

00:21:27.610 --> 00:21:28.710
Cut!

00:21:28.710 --> 00:21:30.510
Okay!

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:36.900
Now, let me wasshoi announce who passed the audition.

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:41.670
The winners are...

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.780
Otoshiro Seira-chan and Saegusa Kii-chan!

00:21:47.030 --> 00:21:48.660
We did it, did it, did it!

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.290
Congratulations.

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:51.410
Good for you.

00:21:51.780 --> 00:21:53.090
Thank you.

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:55.080
Thanky thanky thanks!

00:21:55.080 --> 00:22:01.420
The way you two combined to ace the audition was so fresh, wasshoi!

00:22:01.860 --> 00:22:04.620
How much fun you were having really shone through.

00:22:04.620 --> 00:22:08.050
If I was <i>do</i> today, Seira-chan would've been <i>re</i>.

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:10.730
It was fun!

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:13.560
Let's enter an audition together again sometime.

00:22:13.560 --> 00:22:14.720
Yeah!

00:22:15.270 --> 00:22:16.740
A choco-choco one.

00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:57.820
This week's Aikatsu Aphorism!

00:23:58.870 --> 00:24:01.550
Coming up with a drama scenario was really fun.

00:24:01.550 --> 00:24:04.870
The idea you came up with looks like it'll end up being really cute.

00:24:04.870 --> 00:24:07.430
I'm looking forward to Seira-chan and Kii-chan's performances.

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:09.920
Chocolate gives you ideas!

00:24:11.260 --> 00:24:14.640
Who are those three who are only walking on that white line?

00:24:14.640 --> 00:24:15.820
Powa Powa Puririn!

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:18.430
Everyone, PowaPuri activities are about to start!

00:24:18.860 --> 00:24:20.290
Next time on Aikatsu!

00:24:20.290 --> 00:24:21.710
The Rumored PowaPuri. {or much-, but what are you thinking even}

00:24:21.710 --> 00:24:24.140
Always passionate, idol activities!
